{
  "abstract": "<a href=\"https://sangerinstitute.blog/2026/09/30/six-facts-about-the-gut-microbiome/\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"Six facts about the gut microbiome\"><img alt=\"Microbes from the gut under a high-powered microscope\" class=\"webfeedsFeaturedVisual wp-post-image\" height=\"808\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/sangerinstitute.blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Inside-the-gut_1440-808.jpg?fit=1440%2C808&amp;ssl=1\" style=\"display: block; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 5px;\" width=\"1440\" /></a><p>Deep inside the body, a hidden world of trillions of microbes is constantly at work. Here, we highlight research led by Dr Trevor Lawley’s group at the Wellcome Sanger Institute and explore surprising facts about the gut microbiome, revealing how this unseen ecosystem shapes our health.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://sangerinstitute.blog/2026/09/30/six-facts-about-the-gut-microbiome/\">Six facts about the gut microbiome</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://sangerinstitute.blog\">Wellcome Sanger Institute Blog</a>.</p>",
